        "title": "Identifying Correct Statements About a Matrix"
      },
      "question": {
        ":question/problem": "Consider the matrix \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -7 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}].$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $B$ is upper triangular\n- **II.** $B$ is lower triangular\n- **III.** $B-{B}^{T}$ is upper triangular",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true, since all the entries below the main diagonal equal to zero:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -7 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false, since $B$ has non-zero entries above the main diagonal:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -7 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false, since the result of $B-{B}^{T}$ has non-zero entries below the main diagonal:\n\n$$\nB-{B}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 0 & -7 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\".",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
